OL,3,GNEWSAApplication to use site to store
OL,4,Aindustrial waste
OL,5,
OL,6,FPlans to use part of a site to store
OL,7,Fcommercial and industrial waste have
OL,8,Fbeen submitted.
OL,10,FThe Guernsey Recycling Group wants to
OL,11,Fchange the use of part of its plant in
OL,12,FLongue Hougue, St Sampson, to accept
OL,13,Fthe waste along with acting as a
OL,14,F"secondary small scale storage support
OL,15,Fsite" to complement its other
OL,16,Ffacilities.
OL,18,FIn its plans submitted to the States,
OL,19,Fthe group said it anticipated 18,000
OL,20,Ftonnes of waste including aggregate,
OL,21,Fcommercial and demolition waste would
OL,22,Fbe received each year.
OL,23,APub: 05-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB Ch Is NewsC  Reg TVF Weather
